1383
01:36:04,770 --> 01:36:05,230
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

1384
01:36:07,771 --> 01:36:08,891
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't remember that about him.

1385
01:36:09,531 --> 01:36:10,712
[SPEAKER_00]: He had a couple good years.

1386
01:36:10,892 --> 01:36:11,732
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, yeah.

1387
01:36:14,473 --> 01:36:17,134
[SPEAKER_01]: But I've had a lot of long balls hit off of him.

1388
01:36:19,355 --> 01:36:20,215
[SPEAKER_02]: Who was the longest?

1389
01:36:22,216 --> 01:36:25,757
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I guess the hardest hit ball that I can remember.

1390
01:36:26,863 --> 01:36:31,887
[SPEAKER_01]: was hit in this fourth game of the World Series in Boston by Enos Slaughter.

1391
01:36:32,828 --> 01:36:34,770
[SPEAKER_01]: He really creamed one, hit one.

1392
01:36:37,292 --> 01:36:46,880
[SPEAKER_01]: He hit one in the, or not in, the bullpens are here, the glitches here, he hit one in, way up in the glitches there.

1393
01:36:47,000 --> 01:36:48,501
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, a real nine down.

1394
01:36:50,002 --> 01:36:50,643
[SPEAKER_00]: After a,

1395
01:36:52,327 --> 01:36:53,868
[SPEAKER_00]: The batter does nail one on you.

1396
01:36:53,928 --> 01:36:56,809
[SPEAKER_00]: Next time up, do you try to move him back a little bit?

1397
01:36:57,469 --> 01:37:01,091
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I never did too much of that.

1398
01:37:01,311 --> 01:37:03,271
[SPEAKER_01]: I threw it one man my last time.

1399
01:37:04,932 --> 01:37:05,912
[SPEAKER_01]: I threw it one man.

1400
01:37:06,573 --> 01:37:08,674
[SPEAKER_01]: When I released the ball, I didn't give a damn.

1401
01:37:09,434 --> 01:37:09,954
[SPEAKER_01]: I threw it.

1402
01:37:10,734 --> 01:37:11,135
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't.

1403
01:37:12,175 --> 01:37:14,436
[SPEAKER_01]: There's two ways to do it.

1404
01:37:14,796 --> 01:37:21,039
[SPEAKER_01]: You can throw to brush a man back, or you can throw to hit him.

1405
01:37:21,119 --> 01:37:22,059
[SPEAKER_01]: I threw this pitch.

1406
01:37:22,685 --> 01:37:25,487
[SPEAKER_01]: By the time it left my hand, I was sorry to how it looked after.

1407
01:37:26,088 --> 01:37:30,711
[SPEAKER_01]: It went behind him, and it hit his grandstand.

1408
01:37:31,932 --> 01:37:38,958
[SPEAKER_01]: It was a boy by the name of Thurman Tucker, a left-hand hitting outfielder for Jimmy Dykes.

1409
01:37:39,278 --> 01:37:46,324
[SPEAKER_01]: When I threw at Tucker, when I downed him, Jimmy Dykes cussed me forever.

1410
01:37:46,344 --> 01:37:51,608
[SPEAKER_01]: There's so many in the world for throwing at this guy with the dark, heavy glasses.

1411
01:37:52,948 --> 01:37:57,510
[SPEAKER_01]: I told him, I said, I told you to read my business, the little history behind it.

1412
01:37:57,990 --> 01:37:59,330
[SPEAKER_01]: We're playing in Chicago.

1413
01:38:00,551 --> 01:38:04,972
[SPEAKER_01]: And Tucker was the kind of hitter that carried his betting average on his sleeve, you know.

1414
01:38:05,672 --> 01:38:10,674
[SPEAKER_01]: And he was base hit crazy.

1415
01:38:12,495 --> 01:38:16,856
[SPEAKER_01]: And later in the ball game, score tied and man on second, he out.

1416
01:38:18,617 --> 01:38:20,197
[SPEAKER_01]: Tucker's catching me flat footed.

1417
01:38:20,257 --> 01:38:21,918
[SPEAKER_01]: He'd already had three hits.

1418
01:38:23,859 --> 01:38:30,381
[SPEAKER_01]: And he bunnied, caught me flat-footed, beat it out, that's four.

1419
01:38:31,701 --> 01:38:37,443
[SPEAKER_01]: And if I had been a manager, I would have fined him the maximum.

1420
01:38:38,103 --> 01:38:43,225
[SPEAKER_01]: For bunnying in that situation, you can't drive in the time right with a bump, with two out.

1421
01:38:44,585 --> 01:38:46,686
[SPEAKER_01]: And I resented that to the day.

1422
01:38:46,706 --> 01:38:51,547
[SPEAKER_01]: When he came to Boston later, I told my catcher, I said,

1423
01:38:53,220 --> 01:38:55,900
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm going to change up, change this thing on Tucker.

1424
01:38:56,361 --> 01:38:59,441
[SPEAKER_01]: I told you about going to freeze the slider on the right-handed and left-handed.

1425
01:38:59,461 --> 01:39:00,521
[SPEAKER_01]: We're going to reverse that.

1426
01:39:01,821 --> 01:39:06,762
[SPEAKER_01]: And I threw the slider in on Tucker.

1427
01:39:07,902 --> 01:39:11,143
[SPEAKER_01]: He hits the prop fly just over the first baseman's head.

1428
01:39:11,323 --> 01:39:14,224
[SPEAKER_01]: It's right in the center of the line here with backspin on it.

1429
01:39:14,764 --> 01:39:16,004
[SPEAKER_01]: That's hit number five.

1430
01:39:17,264 --> 01:39:21,005
[SPEAKER_01]: The next time he came up, I said, here, hit this one.

1431
01:39:21,045 --> 01:39:23,005
[SPEAKER_01]: I threw him kind of one on defense pitches.

1432
01:39:23,902 --> 01:39:27,583
[SPEAKER_01]: He beat it against home plate and it bounced 50 feet in the air.

1433
01:39:28,303 --> 01:39:30,983
[SPEAKER_01]: By the time I caught it, he was already across first base.

1434
01:39:31,003 --> 01:39:32,564
[SPEAKER_01]: That's six hits in a row.

1435
01:39:33,464 --> 01:39:34,364
[SPEAKER_01]: I said, that's enough.

1436
01:39:35,164 --> 01:39:37,204
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't tell anybody or say anything.

1437
01:39:38,084 --> 01:39:39,725
[SPEAKER_01]: I lowered the boom.

1438
01:39:40,505 --> 01:39:47,186
[SPEAKER_01]: But everybody in the ballpark and everybody knew because I did have good control.

1439
01:39:47,206 --> 01:39:48,726
[SPEAKER_01]: They knew it was on first base.

1440
01:39:50,087 --> 01:39:52,287
[SPEAKER_01]: But the reason I didn't like to throw it at anybody

1441
01:39:53,430 --> 01:40:04,659
[SPEAKER_01]: When I was in Kenton, the Yankees had a catcher by the name of White that was always probably given the knockdown sign against our ballplayers.

1442
01:40:04,679 --> 01:40:06,781
[SPEAKER_01]: The knockdown is usually the fist, you know.

1443
01:40:07,501 --> 01:40:10,764
[SPEAKER_01]: And some of us knew what he was doing.

1444
01:40:11,484 --> 01:40:12,305
[SPEAKER_00]: Ordering the pitcher.

1445
01:40:13,306 --> 01:40:15,427
[SPEAKER_01]: And I managed to get past that as you told me.

1446
01:40:16,028 --> 01:40:19,030
[SPEAKER_01]: Told the pitcher ahead of me, there's so-and-so there.

1447
01:40:19,050 --> 01:40:20,311
[SPEAKER_01]: I want you to knock him down.

1448
01:40:20,491 --> 01:40:21,092
[SPEAKER_01]: That's White.

1449
01:40:22,148 --> 01:40:23,689
[SPEAKER_01]: They didn't do it.

1450
01:40:25,150 --> 01:40:30,214
[SPEAKER_01]: And they told me the same thing.

1451
01:40:30,234 --> 01:40:33,756
[SPEAKER_01]: Loosen him up.

1452
01:40:33,916 --> 01:40:35,077
[SPEAKER_01]: I did not throw at him.

1453
01:40:36,118 --> 01:40:37,659
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't throw at him just hurt him.

1454
01:40:38,619 --> 01:40:40,221
[SPEAKER_01]: I threw him high inside.

1455
01:40:40,541 --> 01:40:42,002
[SPEAKER_01]: He backs away like this.

1456
01:40:42,982 --> 01:40:46,485
[SPEAKER_01]: The ball hits his hand against the back of his back and broke three bones.

1457
01:40:47,205 --> 01:40:49,687
[SPEAKER_01]: He didn't play for six weeks after that.

1458
01:40:50,601 --> 01:40:54,042
[SPEAKER_00]: And I didn't like that idea.

1459
01:40:54,763 --> 01:40:59,224
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't mean to damage his career, hurt him in any way.

1460
01:40:59,944 --> 01:41:10,408
[SPEAKER_01]: And I didn't ever like for anybody, if I'm going to throw him out or loosen him up to a degree, I don't want nobody to know it was me.

1461
01:41:11,889 --> 01:41:13,770
[SPEAKER_01]: Then I'll tell you another story.

1462
01:41:14,190 --> 01:41:16,451
[SPEAKER_01]: Vernon Stevens was St. Louis.

1463
01:41:19,897 --> 01:41:26,139
[SPEAKER_01]: Before the war, Vernon Stevens hit a home run off me in the 8th inning, tied the ball game.

1464
01:41:29,841 --> 01:41:35,143
[SPEAKER_01]: In the 10th inning or 11th inning, he hit another home run off me in the 3rd inning, beat me in the ball game.

1465
01:41:36,303 --> 01:41:40,085
[SPEAKER_01]: In the 46th, we was playing the Browns.

1466
01:41:41,446 --> 01:41:42,526
[SPEAKER_01]: I was pitching this day.

1467
01:41:42,566 --> 01:41:47,288
[SPEAKER_01]: Vernon Stevens came over to our clubhouse and he's petting me and feeling my arms and said,

1468
01:41:48,672 --> 01:41:49,572
[SPEAKER_01]: He said, how's your arm?

1469
01:41:49,712 --> 01:41:51,133
[SPEAKER_01]: I said, I'm all right.

1470
01:41:52,233 --> 01:41:52,973
[SPEAKER_01]: He said, well good.

1471
01:41:52,993 --> 01:41:54,234
[SPEAKER_01]: He said, you're pitching today.

1472
01:41:54,274 --> 01:41:55,754
[SPEAKER_01]: He said, I'm kind of in a slump.

1473
01:41:55,774 --> 01:41:58,135
[SPEAKER_01]: He said, I'm glad you're pitching today.

1474
01:41:59,055 --> 01:42:03,496
[SPEAKER_01]: And I told him, my friend, I said, you're my friend, you're my buddy.

1475
01:42:04,436 --> 01:42:16,700
[SPEAKER_01]: But I'm telling you, just like a friend, you keep popping off like that, and I'm going to lower you just like flat as a dry cow chip on the Texas prairie if you keep popping off.

1476
01:42:17,933 --> 01:42:27,596
[SPEAKER_01]: So later in the season, I don't know, I got the second base, got a double, and that's enough to take a picture out there.

1477
01:42:27,616 --> 01:42:29,737
[SPEAKER_01]: Changing pictures, I'm at second.

1478
01:42:29,777 --> 01:42:30,917
[SPEAKER_01]: Burns played short.

1479
01:42:31,737 --> 01:42:32,797
[SPEAKER_01]: I called him over.

1480
01:42:33,538 --> 01:42:38,899
[SPEAKER_01]: I said, I've been promising you something for a long time.

1481
01:42:40,440 --> 01:42:44,941
[SPEAKER_01]: And he had just doubled off the screen in right center field.

1482
01:42:47,069 --> 01:42:49,330
[SPEAKER_01]: I said, I'm going to tell you something.

1483
01:42:50,471 --> 01:42:54,072
[SPEAKER_01]: The next time you come to the bus, I'm telling you like a friend.

1484
01:42:55,693 --> 01:42:56,874
[SPEAKER_01]: I said, you're going down.

1485
01:42:57,154 --> 01:42:58,735
[SPEAKER_01]: I said, I've been promising to you.

1486
01:42:58,855 --> 01:43:01,556
[SPEAKER_01]: And if I don't do it, you're going to think I'm a coward.

1487
01:43:02,516 --> 01:43:03,797
[SPEAKER_01]: I said, you just be ready.

1488
01:43:03,857 --> 01:43:05,017
[SPEAKER_01]: It'll be on the first kick.

1489
01:43:07,999 --> 01:43:10,640
[SPEAKER_01]: Vern gets up and cuts his big stents way down.

1490
01:43:12,891 --> 01:43:13,932
[SPEAKER_01]: I threw it at him right here.

1491
01:43:14,592 --> 01:43:16,733
[SPEAKER_01]: I didn't throw it behind him.

1492
01:43:16,953 --> 01:43:18,313
[SPEAKER_01]: I threw it right here.

1493
01:43:18,333 --> 01:43:24,676
[SPEAKER_01]: He did a back flip, got up pretty fast, turned around and didn't say a word.

1494
01:43:25,617 --> 01:43:27,398
[SPEAKER_00]: But I told him, you know.

1495
01:43:29,659 --> 01:43:32,880
[SPEAKER_00]: How did Tucker react the time you threw behind him?

1496
01:43:32,940 --> 01:43:35,901
